  "limitations": [
    "Both are standalone static ELF files run in a scratch filesystem without shared GStreamer or codec libraries.",
    "Runtime configuration uses the shipped codec pipeline at 1280x720/30; tunnel and TURN disabled, loopback HTTP and local metrics enabled.",
    "ARM64 executes in the ARM64 Docker VM; AMD64 executes through Docker Desktop architecture emulation. These are not native AMD64 performance measurements.",
    "Each codec has about 20 seconds of steady media observation, at least 15 samples and 150 newly decoded frames; this checks real encoding/decoding and shutdown, not network impairment or capture-to-display latency.",
    "H.264 sustains 30 fps; AV1 sustains only 8 fps. The AV1 profile has not met its configured 30 fps and requires a separate encoder/profile investigation before making a real-time performance claim.",
    "Source and browser snapshots have different collection boundaries; their absolute frame deltas must not be subtracted as a packet/frame loss count.",
    "The first ARM64 build began with the unchanged 605a55f bytes just before commit. Final make dist and all four final runtime cases use clean 8d252c3."
  ],
